[[:db/retract 17592186162471 :question/answer-fields 17592186159986] [:db/retract 17592186162471 :question/answer-fields 17592186159994] [:db/retract 17592186162471 :question/answer-fields 17592186159991] [:db/retract 17592186162470 :question/answer-fields 17592186159980] {:db/id 17592186161923 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-ac419645-38ad-5793-9dc4-addab4a7d9d8" "question-b769e8d9-7e36-5efc-b6ab-edadbe2e852d" "question-d0842d5b-e854-58d5-ba21-604088a32084" "question-10c4f1e2-954f-5157-a52e-a25057a3e354"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id 17592186161726 :question/problem "Fill in the blanks so that the following reasoning is correct:\n\nThe notation $3 \\mid 18$ means ![](images/06/06b772f72fe6d6f1ee02bdc961f6438561083573e0e0d9d261c7594cd48e86bc.svg) It is equivalent to the statement that there exists \n![](images/c4/c4ebc4da7c8037d0ca6a752df8a4dc3933918db39ac972e4a9b5068fac834140.svg) such that ![](images/88/88e94f9f45ba18035aaea40fb665ecd374c878f9ac7c44aeb038f2d210c02a28.svg)" :question/worked-solution "The notation $a \\mid b$ means $a$ divides $b.$ So, $3 \\mid 18$ means ![](images/5a/5aaf3d46d0bf568ead42806495080fa6eab9d567aa33d22faeee925233867b0a.svg)\n\nAccording to the definition of integer divisibility, the fact that $a$ divides $b$ means that there exists an integer $k$ such that \n\n$$\nb=a k.\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, $3 \\mid 18$ is equivalent to the statement that there exists $\\bbox[3pt,Gainsboro]{\\color{blue}\\textrm{an integer}}$ $k$ such that $\\bbox[3pt,Gainsboro]{\\color{blue}18 = 3k}.$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186161924 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-1931ec0b-024e-521b-8944-a44a623f0a94" "question-8d23d47f-619a-511e-9eb8-d16f783f2804" "question-0cf83f2b-2669-5b7e-af6d-5b0377bff6b8" "question-4a21913b-5a41-5760-aaf4-e4ed518c2eae" "question-327fb10a-fdb6-5fde-b81d-bde8d0149385"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id 17592186161727 :question/problem "Fill in the blanks so that the following reasoning is correct:\n\nThe notation $5 \\not\\mid 16$ means ![](images/fb/fb6fbc91b2218218acab5a0fe1baed797fc7ece0800c3280bc0d53af6d765ae3.svg) It is equivalent to the statement that for $\\[6pt]$ ![](images/48/48442365817dc8d3a14cc2f5931284b07e8cbfccf0bd2a097f7362f0f97348cb.svg)\n![](images/20/20865eee0320e3c8d4822421723a5a251048e7158888ac6416427f632bcb85b7.svg) we have ![](images/45/45453872ffd37b70f166312cf1aa4c3966437e91dc293ac0db198d895e41821c.svg)" :question/worked-solution "The notation $a \\not\\mid b$ means $a$ does not divide $b.$ So, $5 \\not\\mid 16$ means ![](images/83/833ccbc866a4951df8fa798f0780922c3dc56bff0b2baf1a36711c3f47c9f313.svg)\n\nAccording to the definition of integer divisibility, the fact that $a$ does not divide $b$ means that for any integer $k,$ we have that \n\n$$\nb \\neq a k.\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, $5 \\not\\mid 16$ is equivalent to the statement that for $\\bbox[3pt,Gainsboro]{\\color{blue}\\textrm{ any}}$ $\\bbox[3pt,Gainsboro]{\\color{blue}\\textrm{integer}}$ $k,$ we have $\\bbox[3pt,Gainsboro]{\\color{blue}16 \\neq 5k}.$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186161925 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-57bcbc75-d195-518f-bc0e-7dcf10346726" "question-677c3e63-2822-579f-a67a-69517e4d5770" "question-87475b8f-4c6f-5041-abc0-cc4d71389ee6" "question-e7df593d-9767-5ee4-9c1c-cf41d12d4aeb"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id 17592186161728 :question/problem "Which of the following statements must be true for any integers $x$ and $y?$\n\n- $4 \\mid (6x+9y)$\n\n- $5 \\mid (6x+9y)$\n\n- $3 \\mid (6x+9y)$" :question/worked-solution "The notation $a \\mid b$ means $a$ divides $b.$\n\nAccording to the definition of integer divisibility, the fact that $a$ divides $b$ means that there exists an integer $k$ such that \n\n$$\nb=a k.\n$$\n\n \nWith that in mind, let's examine our statement in turn.\n\n- Statement I is false. For example, if $x=0$ and $y=1,$ we have $6(0)+9(1) = 9,$ which is not divisible by $4.$\n\n- Statement II is false. For example, if $x=1$ and $y=0,$ we have $6(1)+9(0) = 6,$ which is not divisible by $5.$\n\n- Statement III is true. Notice that \n\n$$\n6x+9y = 3(2x+3y).\n$$\n\nSince $x$ and $y$ are integers, $2x+3y$ must be an integer, too. So, $3 \\mid (6x+9y).$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"III only.\"" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "question-ac419645-38ad-5793-9dc4-addab4a7d9d8" :question/id #uuid "ac419645-38ad-5793-9dc4-addab4a7d9d8" :question/math-academy-id "q-221902" :question/problem "Select the correct options in the reasoning below." :question/worked-solution "The notation $a∣b$ means $a$ divides $b.$ So, $4∣12$ means $4\\text{ divides }12.$\n\nAccording to the definition of integer divisibility, the fact that $a$ divides $b$ means that there exists an integer $k$ such that \n\n$$\nb=ak.\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, $4∣12$ is equivalent to the statement that there exists $\\text{an integer}$ $k$ such that $12=4k.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-e4da5663-d130-5d97-a375-3ad78775e77e" "answer-field-f6ecd83c-4a7d-5942-9f19-9559e26dd7b0" "answer-field-e8173600-a897-53d1-bd7c-f66c54077c2c"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-e4da5663-d130-5d97-a375-3ad78775e77e" :answer-field/id #uuid "e4da5663-d130-5d97-a375-3ad78775e77e" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/select :answer-field/correct "answer-3b2804d0-be24-521c-afa9-e8131895290d" :answer-field/choices ["answer-bea957c7-2806-51fe-baae-8bef062d2e9a" "answer-1278745e-9ac1-5d09-b721-84a234f65b51" "answer-3b2804d0-be24-521c-afa9-e8131895290d" "answer-568f62ce-3d7c-5d68-816d-2dc295f00912"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-bea957c7-2806-51fe-baae-8bef062d2e9a" :answer/id #uuid "bea957c7-2806-51fe-baae-8bef062d2e9a" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$12$ divides $4$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-1278745e-9ac1-5d09-b721-84a234f65b51" :answer/id #uui