er-839bd9f5-1964-55fd-9d02-6a1fe894ae4a" :answer/id #uuid "839bd9f5-1964-55fd-9d02-6a1fe894ae4a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "6\\ne 11k" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-327fb10a-fdb6-5fde-b81d-bde8d0149385" :question/id #uuid "327fb10a-fdb6-5fde-b81d-bde8d0149385" :question/math-academy-id "q-221913" :question/problem "Select the correct options in the reasoning below." :question/worked-solution "The notation $a∤b$ means $a$ does not divides $b.$ So, $5∤9$ means $5\\text{ doesn't divide }9.$\n\nAccording to the definition of integer divisibility, the fact that $a$ does not divide $b$ means that for any integer $k,$ we have that \n\n$$\nb\\ne ak.\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, $5∤9$ is equivalent to the statement that $\\text{for any}$ $\\text{integer}$ $k,$ we have $9\\ne 5k.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-5882d1cd-fd39-5b71-94f1-a66f4a113ce6" "answer-field-11755818-81fa-5a9c-85d1-78977f4deeeb" "answer-field-f9f1a640-2908-5f41-b600-e7615558bb3c" "answer-field-49663b59-58e9-51b4-a533-be7fa9e1ac4e"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-5882d1cd-fd39-5b71-94f1-a66f4a113ce6" :answer-field/id #uuid "5882d1cd-fd39-5b71-94f1-a66f4a113ce6" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/select :answer-field/correct "answer-7e6fe643-86dd-5892-b2a3-910c04d36021" :answer-field/choices ["answer-adc35665-60bd-5272-a709-e838cf8b0f7d" "answer-7e6fe643-86dd-5892-b2a3-910c04d36021" "answer-8bdd8ee0-be22-5ab4-95ff-d2e550bd99a4" "answer-6dda37ca-f496-526a-a805-2f57fb422821"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-adc35665-60bd-5272-a709-e838cf8b0f7d" :answer/id #uuid "adc35665-60bd-5272-a709-e838cf8b0f7d" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$5$ divides $9$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-7e6fe643-86dd-5892-b2a3-910c04d36021" :answer/id #uuid "7e6fe643-86dd-5892-b2a3-910c04d36021" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$5$