nswer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "number" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-49663b59-58e9-51b4-a533-be7fa9e1ac4e" :answer-field/id #uuid "49663b59-58e9-51b4-a533-be7fa9e1ac4e" :answer-field/key "field-4" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/select :answer-field/correct "answer-9a954823-8efb-5a32-8695-510b68cc731d" :answer-field/choices ["answer-f85b1c69-bce4-58f7-ab35-37a4cec814fb" "answer-9a954823-8efb-5a32-8695-510b68cc731d"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-f85b1c69-bce4-58f7-ab35-37a4cec814fb" :answer/id #uuid "f85b1c69-bce4-58f7-ab35-37a4cec814fb" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "5\\ne 9k" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-9a954823-8efb-5a32-8695-510b68cc731d" :answer/id #uuid "9a954823-8efb-5a32-8695-510b68cc731d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "9\\ne 5k" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-57bcbc75-d195-518f-bc0e-7dcf10346726" :question/id #uuid "57bcbc75-d195-518f-bc0e-7dcf10346726" :question/math-academy-id "q-221924" :question/problem "Which of the following statements must be true for any integers $x$ and $y?$\n\n- $2∣(60x-45y)$\n- $9∣(60x-45y)$\n- $5∣(60x-45y)$" :question/worked-solution "The notation $a∣b$ means $a$ divides $b.$\n\nAccording to the definition of integer divisibility, the fact that $a$ divides $b$ means that there exists an integer $k$ such that \n\n$$\nb=ak.\n$$\n\n \nWith that in mind, let's examine our statement in turn.\n\n- Statement I is false. For example, if $x=0$ and $y=1,$ we have $60(0)-45(1)=-45,$ which is not divisible by $2.$\n\n- Statement II is false. For example, if $x=1$ and $y=1,$ we have $60(1)-45(1)=15,$ which is not divisible by $9.$\n\n- Statement III is true. Notice that \n\n$$\n60x-45y=5(12x-9y).\n$$\n\nSince $x$ and $y$ are integers, $12x-9y$ must be an integer, too. So, $5∣(60x-45y).$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \" III only.\"" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-acfbeec0-d695-5669-98f1-e0c98afcce16"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-acfbeec0-d695-5669-98f1-e0c98afcce16" :answer-field/id #uuid "acfbeec0-d695-5669-98f1-e0c98afcce16" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-417cda45-5deb-5a71-9253-a3a0df6b4f58" :answer-field/choices ["answer-47984d83-a59d-5c9e-b0ed-fecc2f753d7c" "answer-ad69e9c1-1ebb-560c-9e77-00f1fd732382" "answer-852beed3-2c95-5176-a9ae-504c72adf621" "answer-8c3d09f0-2c82-592d-bfc6-7d6d6263bbc0" "answer-417cda45-5deb-5a71-9253-a3a0df6b4f58"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-47984d83-a59d-5c9e-b0ed-fecc2f753d7c" :answer/id #uuid "47984d83-a59d-5c9e-b0ed-fecc2f753d7c" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I and II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-ad69e9c1-1ebb-560c-9e77-00f1fd732382" :answer/id #uuid "ad69e9c1-1ebb-560c-9e77-00f1fd732382" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-852beed3-2c95-5176-a9ae-504c72adf621" :answer/id #uuid "852beed3-2c95-5176-a9ae-504c72adf621" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II and III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-8c3d09f0-2c82-592d-bfc6-7d6d6263bbc0" :answer/id #uuid "8c3d09f0-2c82-592d-bfc6-7d6d6263bbc0" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-417cda45-5deb-5a71-9253-a3a0df6b4f58" :answer/id #uuid "417cda45-5deb-5a71-9253-a3a0df6b4f58" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-677c3e63-2822-579f-a67a-69517e4d5770" :question/id #uuid "677c3e63-2822-579f-a67a-69517e4d5770" :question/math-academy-id "q-221927" :question/problem "Which of the following statements must be true for any integers $x$ and $y?$\n\n- $5∣(8x+6y)$\n- $2∣(8x+6y)$\n- $3∣(8x+6y)$" :question/worked-solution "The notation $a∣b$ means $a$ divides $b.$\n\nAccording to the definition of integer divisibility, the fact that $a$ divides $b$ means that there exists an integer $k$ such that \n\n$$\nb=ak.\n$$\n\n \nWith that in mind, let's examine our statement in turn.\n\n- Statement I is false. For example, if $x=1$ and $y=0,$ we have $8(1)+6(0)=8,$ which is not divisible by $5.$\n\n- Statement II is true. Notice that \n\n$$\n8x+6y=2(4x+3y).\n$$\n\nSince $x$ and $y$ are integers, $4x+3y$ must be an integer, too. So, $2∣(8x+6y).$\n\n- Statement III is false. For example, if $x=1$ and $y=0,$ we have $8(1)+6(0)=8,$ which is not divisible by $3.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II only.\"" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-a12c464c-0427-5713-9930-41823b0ab244"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-a12c464c-0427-5713-9930-41823b0ab244" :answer-field/id #uuid "a12c464c-0427-5713-9930-41823b0ab244" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-2b69be42-2b62-50f4-b509-868d1c9cc7e6" :answer-field/choices ["answer-2272ac5e-7d0f-56a3-ac97-994658312363" "answer-d24532ad-ad89-5f9d-ae39-b1ba94e8bf28" "answer-990a7a87-e36c-55af-8157-7626787e9d06" "answer-2b69be42-2b62-50f4-b509-868d1c9cc7e6" "answer-a6c277c5-5a7b-5cdc-9f28-011af8d694cd"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-2272ac5e-7d0f-56a3-ac97-994658312363" :answer/id #uuid "2272ac5e-7d0f-56a3-ac97-994658312363" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-d24532ad-ad89-5f9d-ae39-b1ba94e8bf28" :answer/id #uuid "d24532ad-ad89-5f9d-ae39-b1ba94e8bf28" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I, II and III" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-990a7a87-e36c-55af-8157-7626787e9d06" :answer/id #uuid "990a7a87-e36c-55af-8157-7626787e9d06" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II and III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-2b69be42-2b62-50f4-b509-868d1c9cc7e6" :answer/id #uuid "2b69be42-2b62-50f4-b509-868d1c9cc7e6" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-a6c277c5-5a7b-5cdc-9f28-011af8d694cd" :answer/id #uuid "a6c277c5-5a7b-5cdc-9f28-011af8d694cd" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186162470 :question/problem "Which of the following statements must be true for any integers $x$ and $y?$\n\n- $6∣(42x+24y)$\n- $7∣(42x+24y)$\n- $2∣(42x+24y)$" :question/worked-solution "The notation $a∣b$ means $a$ divides $b.$\n\nAccording to the definition of integer divisibility, the fact that $a$ divides $b$ means that there exists an integer $k$ such that \n\n$$\nb=ak.\n$$\n\n \nWith that in mind, let's examine our statement in turn.\n\n- Statement I is true. Notice that \n\n$$\n42x+24y=6(7x+4y).\n$$\n\nSince $x$ and $y$ are integers, $7x+4y$ must be an integer, too. So, $6∣(42x+24y).$\n\n- Statement II is false. For example, if $x=0$ and $y=1,$ we have $42(0)+24(1)=24,$ which is not divisible by $7.$\n\n- Statement III is true. Notice that \n\n$$\n42x+24y=2(21x+12y).\n$$\n\nSince $x$ and $y$ are integers, $21x+12y$ must be an integer, too. So, $2∣(42x+24y).$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and III only.\"" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-ce80592a-d65e-5a24-ac6e-46f8654903b7"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-ce80592a-d65e-5a24-ac6e-46f8654903b7" :answer-field/id #uuid "ce80592a-d65e-5a24-ac6e-46f8654903b7" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-8d91791d-f4c6-51bc-b004-2d1b8f7e6d98" :answer-field/choices ["answer-d1d961f4-d0e1-5413-9854-bf9e8c1f9ccb" "answer-8d91791d-f4c6-51bc-b004-2d1b8f7e6d98" "answer-4e16abfb-19a2-5993-ba56-d6ea9e861af4" "answer-077fe147-bb8c-5245-adec-2f208cac3d00" "answer-a3ada6aa-c40c-51ac-b29e-9b542bd9b596"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-d1d961f4-d0e1-5413-9854-bf9e8c1f9ccb" :answer/id #uuid "d1d961f4-d0e1-5413-9854-bf9e8c1f9ccb" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I and II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-8d91791d-f4c6-51bc-b004-2d1b8f7e6d98" :answer/id #uuid "8d91791d-f4c6-51bc-b004-2d1b8f7e6d98" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I and III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-4e16abfb-19a2-5993-ba56-d6ea9e861af4" :answer/id #uuid "4e16abfb-19a2-5993-ba56-d6ea9e861af4" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I, II, and III" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-077fe147-bb8c-5245-adec-2f208cac3d00" :answer/id #uuid "077fe147-bb8c-5245-adec-2f208cac3d00" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-a3ada6aa-c40c-51ac-b29e-9b542bd9b596" :answer/id #uuid "a3ada6aa-c40c-51ac-b29e-9b542bd9b596" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-87475b8f-4c6f-5041-abc0-cc4d71389ee6" :question/id #uuid "87475b8f-4c6f-5041-abc0-cc4d71389ee6" :question/math-academy-id "q-221928" :question/problem "Which of the following statements must be true for any integers $x$ and $y?$\n\n- $3$ divides $(8x+6y)$\n- $2$ divides $(8x+6y)$\n- $4$ divides $(8x+6y)$" :question/worked-solution "The notation $a∣b$ means $a$ divides $b.$\n\nAccording to the definition of integer divisibility, the fact that $a$ divides $b$ means that there exists an integer $k$ such that \n\n$$\nb=ak.\n$$\n\n \nWith that in mind, let's examine our statement in turn.\n\n- Statement I is false. For example, if $x=1$ and $y=0,$ we have $8(1)+6(0)=8,$ which is not divisible by $3.$\n\n- Statement II is true. Notice that \n\n$$\n8x+6y=2(4x+3y).\n$$\n\nSince $x$ and $y$ are integers, $4x+3y$ must be an integer, too. So, $2$ divides $(8x+6y).$\n\n- Statement III is false. For example, if $x=0$ and $y=1,$ we have $8(0)+6(1)=6,$ which is not divisible by $4.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II only.\"" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-7a2706c2-73db-5a55-a6d5-9289ff01e1ac"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-7a2706c2-73db-5a55-a6d5-9289ff01e1ac" :answer-field/id #uuid "7a2706c2-73db-5a55-a6d5-9289ff01e1ac" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-8fef28c7-794b-5733-a1fe-0753d63b034f" :answer-field/choices ["answer-e8e88934-c419-5f9c-aeef-75af01952dad" "answer-8e4b945a-cfab-5802-9826-b499d69bf07c" "answer-7c4c39ff-1830-583c-bfbe-3b1923927d10" "answer-8fef28c7-794b-5733-a1fe-0753d63b034f" "answer-bf65c1a0-9ca7-5e13-851e-5b8ebe65ec4d"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-e8e88934-c419-5f9c-aeef-75af01952dad" :answer/id #uuid "e8e88934-c419-5f9c-aeef-75af01952dad" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I and II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-8e4b945a-cfab-5802-9826-b499d69bf07c" :answer/id #uuid "8e4b945a-cfab-5802-9826-b499d69bf07c" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-7c4c39ff-1830-583c-bfbe-3b1923927d10" :answer/id #uuid "7c4c39ff-1830-583c-bfbe-3b1923927d10" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II and III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-8fef28c7-794b-5733-a1fe-0753d63b034f" :answer/id #uuid "8fef28c7-794b-5733-a1fe-0753d63b034f" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-bf65c1a0-9ca7-5e13-851e-5b8ebe65ec4d" :answer/id #uuid "bf65c1a0-9ca7-5e13-851e-5b8ebe65ec4d" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-e7df593d-9767-5ee4-9c1c-cf41d12d4aeb" :question/id #uuid "e7df593d-9767-5ee4-9c1c-cf41d12d4aeb" :question/math-academy-id "q-221932" :question/problem "Which of the following statements must be true for any integers $x$ and $y?$\n\n- $6$ divides $(24x+30y)$\n- $3$ divides $(24x+30y)$\n- $5$ divides $(24x+30y)$" :question/worked-solution "The notation $a∣b$ means $a$ divides $b.$\n\nAccording to the definition of integer divisibility, the fact that $a$ divides $b$ means that there exists an integer $k$ such that \n\n$$\nb=ak.\n$$\n\n \nWith that in mind, let's examine our statement in turn.\n\n- Statement I is true. Notice that \n\n$$\n24x+30y=6(4x+5y).\n$$\n\nSince $x$ and $y$ are integers, $4x+5y$ must be an integer, too. So, $6$ divides $(24x+30y).$\n\n- Statement II is true. Notice that \n\n$$\n24x+30y=3(8x+10y).\n$$\n\nSince $x$ and $y$ are integers, $8x+10y$ must be an integer, too. So, $3$ divides $(24x+30y).$\n\n- Statement III is false. For example, if $x=-1$ and $y=1,$ we have $24(-1)+30(1)=6,$ which is not divisible by $5.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \" I and II only.\"" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-9e816fd2-d475-50e3-9740-ad25b3cf43dd"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-9e816fd2-d475-50e3-9740-ad25b3cf43dd" :answer-field/id #uuid "9e816fd2-d475-50e3-9740-ad25b3cf43dd" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-59b4b9f4-8423-53e2-86a4-af6400356c4b" :answer-field/choices ["answer-6a8a7ed1-a714-5a9e-8cca-5f810fde21a7" "answer-59b4b9f4-8423-53e2-86a4-af6400356c4b" "answer-c203c295-5f0c-5cb5-a465-33ad0fef7926" "answer-070efb65-293c-5069-a098-e98293361bfb" "answer-262239e2-54ef-5ba5-9c45-43c82a528c79"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-6a8a7ed1-a714-5a9e-8cca-5f810fde21a7" :answer/id #uuid "6a8a7ed1-a714-5a9e-8cca-5f810fde21a7" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I  only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-59b4b9f4-8423-53e2-86a4-af6400356c4b" :answer/id #uuid "59b4b9f4-8423-53e2-86a4-af6400356c4b" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I and II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-c203c295-5f0c-5cb5-a465-33ad0fef7926" :answer/id #uuid "c203c295-5f0c-5cb5-a465-33ad0fef7926" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I and III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-070efb65-293c-5069-a098-e98293361bfb" :answer/id #uuid "070efb65-293c-5069-a098-e98293361bfb" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II and III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-262239e2-54ef-5ba5-9c45-43c82a528c79" :answer/id #uuid "262239e2-54ef-5ba5-9c45-43c82a528c79" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186163373 :tutorial/content "Suppose $a$ and $b$ are integers where $a\\neq 0.$ We say that $\\boldsymbol a$ **divides** $\\boldsymbol b$ and write \n\n$$\na\\mid b\n$$\n\nif there exists an integer $k$ such that\n\n$$\nb = ka.\n$$\n\nWe can write this more formally as follows:\n\n$$\na\\mid b \\qquad \\Leftrightarrow\\qquad \\exists k \\in \\mathbb Z, b = ka\n$$\n\nFor example, $2\\mid 8$ because there exists an integer ${\\color{blue}{k}} = {\\color{blue}{4}}$ such that\n\n$$\n8 = {\\color{blue}{4}}\\cdot 2.\n$$" :db/ensure [:tutorial/validate]} {:db/id 17592186163374 :tutorial/content "We have the following definition of integer divisibility. \n\n$$\na\\mid b \\qquad \\Leftrightarrow\\qquad \\exists k \\in \\mathbb Z, b = ka\n$$\n\nIf $a$ **does not divide** $b,$ we write $a\\not\\mid b.$ Therefore, by negating the two statements above, we get the following equivalence:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}¬(a∣b)\\, & ⇔\\,¬(∃k\\in Z,b=ka) \\\\ a∤b\\, & ⇔\\,∀k\\in Z,b\\ne ka\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThus, $a\\not\\mid b$ means that $b \\neq ak$ *for all* integers $k.$\n\nFor example, $3\\not \\mid 8$ because there does not exist an integer ${\\color{red}{k_2}}$ such that\n\n$$\n8 = {\\color{red}{k_2}}\\cdot 3.\n$$" :db/ensure [:tutorial/validate]} {:db/id 17592186162213 :activity/expected-seconds 420.0 :db/ensure [:activity/validate]}]
